Meetings gain a lifecycle owner: `POST /meetings` (V19) takes a required `managed_by` field (`"wire"` or `"google_calendar"`, echoed in meeting responses; immutable after creation, not part of updates). `google_calendar`-managed meetings can only be created, updated, deleted, link-refreshed and have invitations changed by calendar-integration (OAuth) callers; Wire clients (cookie/token with a connection) get `403 managed-by-calendar`. Meeting mutation routes now accept OAuth bearer callers (connection header is optional), enabling pure-bearer clients such as the calendar add-on.
